#!perl
use v5.36;
use Permutl::CLI;

exit Permutl::CLI::main(@ARGV);

__END__

=head1 NAME

permutl - measure how many mutants the tests of a Perl project detect

=head1 SYNOPSIS

    permutl [run] [options]
    permutl list
    permutl show ID
    permutl exec ID -- COMMAND [ARGUMENT...]
    permutl merge FILE...
    permutl mutators
    permutl --help

=head1 DESCRIPTION

C<permutl> runs in the root of a distribution, or in the directory that C<--root> names.
C<permutl --help> lists every option.
L<Permutl> describes the configuration file, the reports, and the limits.

